    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis from the ileal conduit, corrected (E87.22)</content>. Bicarbonate 24 mmol/L and chloride 106 mmol/L on sodium bicarbonate; creatinine 1.10 mg/dL, stable. [S]<list><item>Continue sodium bicarbonate 650 mg twice daily.</item><item>Chemistry at one year after surgery, then yearly if stable.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bladder cancer after radical cystoprostatectomy, pT2a N0, no evidence of disease (Z85.51)</content>. No symptoms or signs of recurrence nine months after surgery. [S]<list><item>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis with a urographic phase in three months, at one year after surgery.</item><item>Written survivorship care plan given today: the surveillance schedule, symptoms to report (blood from the stoma, flank or bone pain, weight loss, a bulge by the stoma), and who to call.</item><item>Urology review with the CT.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Ileal conduit urostomy (Z93.6)</content>. Stoma healthy; no hernia. [S]<list><item>Continue the current appliance; stoma nurse review yearly or for any problem.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Chemistry with creatinine, chloride, and bicarbonate</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months in the first year after diversion, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 1.10 mg/dL, eGFR 74; chloride 106, bicarbonate 24 mmol/L on treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Vitamin B12</td><td>Yearly from two to three years after an ileal diversion</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline normal six months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis (with urographic phase)</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months for 2 to 3 years after cystectomy, then yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At one year after surgery, in three months; the urographic phase covers the upper tracts</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Upper-tract imaging (renal ultrasound or CT urography)</td><td>Every 6 months to year 3, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Renal ultrasound three months ago without hydronephrosis; next with the CT</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Stoma and peristomal skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Healthy</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Parastomal and incisional hernia</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sodium bicarbonate: tolerance and sodium load</td><td>Every visit on alkali therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No bloating; blood pressure 128/76 mm Hg; no edema</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine urine culture of conduit urine</td><td>Only for fever, flank pain, or other signs of infection</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Bacteria are expected in conduit urine; no symptoms today</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urethral wash cytology</td><td>Periodically if the urethra is retained and at high risk</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Urethral margin negative and no prostatic urethral involvement</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Survivorship care plan, fluid intake, and activity</td><td>After treatment; fluids and activity every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Written plan given; about 2 liters of fluid a day; walking 30 minutes most days</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Leak-free urostomy appliance with healthy peristomal skin. Outcome by 1977-04-07: Appliance refitted with a convex wafer at the consultation; no leaks in the two months after the refit and skin healed [S]</item><item>Stable kidney function (creatinine within 0.3 mg/dL of the post-operative baseline) and bicarbonate 22 mmol/L or more. Outcome by 1977-07-07: Creatinine 1.10 mg/dL; bicarbonate 24 mmol/L on sodium bicarbonate [S]</item><item>Regain stamina after surgery: walk 30 minutes a day and regain weight. Outcome by 1977-04-07: Walking 30 minutes most days; weight up 1.1 kg since the first visit [S]</item><item>Written survivorship surveillance schedule in place, shared between urology and primary care. Outcome by 1977-07-07: Schedule given; CT due at one year after surgery [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Holzbeierlein J, et al. Treatment of Non-Metastatic Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer: AUA/ASCO/SUO Guideline (2017; Amended 2020, 2024). J Urol 2024;212(1):3-10 (2024); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Bladder Cancer (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, urologic cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: CT and urology review in three months, at one year after surgery. Primary care at the same time with chemistry. [S]</paragraph></text>

